xnu 0195: the draw-state expansion is opt-in until the rewrite is right

Measured on one kernel: with the expansion off (the pre-0195 kernel did it with
gpunostate=1) the 71-dword stream completes in 13 ms and only the 168-dword one
that carries the draw-state group wedges; with the expansion on (0193) the
71-dword stream stops answering as well, so the rewritten stream or its patched
nested packet is wrong. Keep the expansion off by default and let gpunostate=1
turn it on again once the rewrite is right.

--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
@@ -2787,7 +2787,14 @@
 mondrian_gpu_uc_nostate(void)
 {
 #ifdef MONDRIAN_CP_PROFILE
-	return mondrian_uc_nostate;
+	/*
+	 * The draw-state expansion (0193) is off unless gpunostate=1 asks for it:
+	 * with it on, even the 71-dword stream that completes on its own stops
+	 * answering, so the rewrite is not right yet. Off, that stream keeps
+	 * working and only the one carrying the group wedges (0191 keeps the
+	 * system alive through it).
+	 */
+	return mondrian_uc_nostate == 0 ? 1 : 0;
 #else
 	return 1;
 #endif
